# Ten conjugates through the marked HS involution

The displayed elementary subgroup of order32 has ten conjugates under the
centralizer of the marked inner involution. The two previously verified
centralizer generators and a specified outer involution permute the ten
rows. Each noninitial row intersects the initial row in exactly four
permutations. All finite equations are checked in the kernel on the
original degree100 carrier; the discovery data is not a proof premise.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith12.6.12, printed pp.825--826.
